<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐδηλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐδᾱλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> priv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φιδεῖν</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making unseen, annihilating, destructive</i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, as epith. of Arcs and Athena, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.897
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				880
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.455
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				109
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠελίοιο ἔργ᾽ ἀΐδηλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					10.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐδαλος τύχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					240.5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.487
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πότμος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.150
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λως,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλεθρίως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.220
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>unseen , unknown, obscure</i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.318
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				756
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.102
			</span></i>, al.; <i>unforeseen</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				298
			</span></i>; <i>formless</i>,<i><span class="en">
				4.681
			</span></i>; <i>unsubstantial</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					727
				</span></i>
			; as epith. of Hades, <i>dark, gloomy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				608
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
